.TH KRONEIN-TX "1" "October 2026" "kronein-tx v31.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kronein-tx \- manual page for kronein-tx v31.1.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kronein-tx
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,<hex-tx> \/\fR[\fI\,commands\/\fR]
.br
.B kronein-tx
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,-create \/\fR[\fI\,commands\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kronein Core kronein\-tx utility version v31.1.0
.PP
The kronein\-tx tool is used for creating and modifying Kronein transactions.
.PP
kronein\-tx can be used with "<hex\-tx> [commands]" to update a hex\-encoded Kronein transaction, or with "\-create [commands]" to create a hex\-encoded Kronein transaction.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB\-create\fR
.IP
Create new, empty TX.
.HP
\fB\-help\fR
.IP
Print this help message and exit (also \fB\-h\fR or \-?)
.HP
\fB\-json\fR
.IP
Select JSON output
.HP
\fB\-txid\fR
.IP
Output only the hex\-encoded transaction id of the resultant transaction.
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Print version and exit
.PP
Chain selection options:
.HP
\fB\-chain=\fR<chain>
.IP
Use the chain <chain> (default: main). Allowed values: main, testnet4,
signet, regtest
.HP
\fB\-signet\fR
.IP
Use the signet chain. Equivalent to \fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,signet\/\fR. Note that the network
is defined by the \fB\-signetchallenge\fR parameter
.HP
\fB\-signetchallenge\fR
.IP
Blocks must provide a Taproot witness satisfying this P2TR scriptPubKey
(only for signet networks; defaults to the project Signet
challenge)
.HP
\fB\-signetseednode\fR
.IP
Specify a seed node for the signet network, in the hostname[:port]
format, e.g. sig.net:1234 (may be used multiple times)
.HP
\fB\-testnet4\fR
.IP
Use the testnet4 chain. Equivalent to \fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,testnet4\/\fR.
.PP
Commands:
.IP
delin=N
.IP
Delete input N from TX
.IP
delout=N
.IP
Delete output N from TX
.IP
in=TXID:VOUT(:SEQUENCE_NUMBER)
.IP
Add input to TX
.IP
locktime=N
.IP
Set TX lock time to N
.IP
outaddr=VALUE:ADDRESS
.IP
Add address\-based output to TX
.IP
outdata=[VALUE:]DATA
.IP
Add data\-based output to TX
.IP
outscript=VALUE:SCRIPT
.IP
Add raw script output to TX.
.IP
replaceable(=N)
.IP
Sets Replace\-By\-Fee (RBF) opt\-in sequence number for input N. If N is
not provided, the command attempts to opt\-in all available inputs
for RBF. If the transaction has no inputs, this option is
ignored.
